WEBVTT

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:10.810
<v Speaker 1>Hey, this is Justin Gary here at day two of the Magic the Gathering World Championships. I'm here with Cole Swannack, who is the youngest player here at the World Championships. Cole, how old are you?</v>

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:11.790
<v Speaker 2>I'm 15.</v>

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.390
<v Speaker 1>Alright, and now this is not your first World Championships. How many times have you been?</v>

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.240
<v Speaker 2>Here, this is my third world.</v>

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.010
<v Speaker 1>Alright. And how is it going for you?</v>

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.610
<v Speaker 2>Not too bad, not too bad.</v>

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.600
<v Speaker 1>Yeah, what's your?</v>

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:22.990
<v Speaker 2>Record for two at the moment.</v>

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.870
<v Speaker 1>OK. And you just finished your draft, you feel confident, you think you'll be able to do well with.</v>

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.110
<v Speaker 2>It it's alright, it's a good enough Dick to produce a decent record.</v>

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:44.700
<v Speaker 1>Now it's pretty impressive rate for somebody of your age to come the world's even once you've been able to do it three times. I know there's a lot of people out there around your age that really would love to see, you know, themselves in this position. What do you think? What do you what kind of advice do you have for people out there?</v>

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:51.580
<v Speaker 2>Just keep practicing, play a lot of Moto motos. Good magic online. Yep, that's where I do most of.</v>

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:53.560
<v Speaker 1>My competitors, The pairings</v>

00:00:55.170 --> 00:01:00.940
<v Speaker 1>rounds coming up, and Cole's gonna have to go. We'll keep an eye on him and everybody else here at the Magic Gathering World Championships.</v>

